WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.280
In 2001 a capsule was approved for a leukaemia.

2
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.960
It was aimed at one enzyme.

3
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:16.300
But about five hundred human kinases hold ATP in nearly the same pocket.

4
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.020
A kinase is an enzyme that moves a phosphate onto a protein.

5
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:28.020
Around 1990, a molecule shaped to jam one pocket was expected to jam dozens.

6
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.940
So how do you drug just one?

7
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.280
The molecule that worked is called imatinib.

8
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.800
It hit a short list of kinases, not hundreds.

9
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.420
One of them is BCR-ABL.

10
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:48.540
This fused kinase is always on, and it drives chronic myeloid leukaemia.

11
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.240
Imatinib sits in its ATP pocket and inhibits it.

12
00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.440
Most leukaemia cells do not get through a period without it.

13
00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.120
Normal cells do.

14
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:06.463
Some patients in the early imatinib trials, mostly those with advanced disease, got

15
00:01:06.463 --> 00:01:08.243
well and then relapsed.

16
00:01:09.203 --> 00:01:14.343
In one laboratory, a scientist read the BCR-ABL gene from their blood.

17
00:01:15.263 --> 00:01:19.083
In several patients, one DNA letter had

18
00:01:19.883 --> 00:01:22.143
changed. ACT had become ATT.

19
00:01:23.203 --> 00:01:27.803
That replaces threonine at position 315 with isoleucine.

20
00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:34.447
Threonine 315 is one of the contacts that hold imatinib in its pocket.

21
00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:36.867
Isoleucine is bulkier.

22
00:01:37.287 --> 00:01:38.787
It cannot make that contact.

23
00:01:39.227 --> 00:01:41.007
So the drug no longer binds.

24
00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:45.487
But the enzyme does not need this residue for its own reaction.

25
00:01:45.987 --> 00:01:47.367
The kinase keeps working.

26
00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.740
A relapse looks like a failure of the idea.

27
00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.680
Read it as an experiment instead.

28
00:01:55.580 --> 00:02:00.340
To survive, the leukaemia changed the one position the drug depended on.

29
00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.700
It left the rest of the enzyme alone.

30
00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.980
That is strong evidence that the drug had been working through BCR-ABL, and that the

31
00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.560
leukaemia still needed it.

32
00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:18.463
The relapse also wrote the specification for the next drug: grip ABL without needing

33
00:02:18.463 --> 00:02:25.583
residue 315. Ponatinib was built with a slim carbon-carbon triple bond where the

34
00:02:25.583 --> 00:02:27.743
isoleucine side chain sticks out.

35
00:02:28.303 --> 00:02:30.123
It inhibits the mutant kinase.

36
00:02:31.123 --> 00:02:36.023
Keep this rule. A relapse writes the specification for the next drug.
